# Self-pin patterns for the audit-harness repo itself.
#
# Per IEP Convergence Debt Plan Priority 3 (iah-self-pin / bd_000-projects-itpl).
# The default harness-hash patterns target consumer-repo artifacts (.feature
# files, architecture rule configs, coverage threshold configs) — none of which
# exist in audit-harness's own tree because audit-harness IS the policy enforcer.
# This file extends the pin scope to cover audit-harness's policy enforcement
# surface: the deterministic scripts that gate every consumer repo.
#
# Any byte change to a pinned file requires re-running `bash scripts/harness-hash.sh --init`
# and committing the regenerated .harness-hash. The CI gate at .github/workflows/ci.yml
# (no longer tolerant — see iep-P3 iah-self-pin) refuses the diff otherwise.

# Deterministic gate scripts (the policy)
scripts/*.sh
scripts/*.py

# CLI dispatcher (thin per design rule 1; pinned so the dispatcher's command
# routing can't drift silently from the scripts it dispatches to)
bin/audit-harness.js

# This pin-extra-patterns file itself — preventing silent edits to the
# self-pinning scope. Bootstrapping note: the first --init that runs with this
# file in place will hash it into the manifest; subsequent edits require re-init.
.harness-hash-extra-patterns
